Subject: [PATCH] camss: add the SM8150 2-phase CSIPHY v1.1 variant

The SM8150 CSIPHY is a 2-phase v1.1 part: its control block sits at
base+0x800 instead of base+0x140, its lane blocks are at 0x000/0x200/0x400
(data) and 0x700 (clock) instead of 0x40*n, and it has its own reset, IRQ and
lane-enable tables.  Recovered from the vendor kernel of the Redmi K20 Pro
(see ../../drivers/csiphy_v1_1_tables.h and analysis/csiphy-v1-1-real.md).

Files to add to the kernel tree:
  drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-2ph-1-1.c
  drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-2ph-1-1.h
  drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/csiphy_v1_1_tables.h

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/Makefile b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/Makefile
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/Makefile
@@
 qcom-camss-objs += camss-csiphy-2ph-1-0.o
+qcom-camss-objs += camss-csiphy-2ph-1-1.o
 qcom-camss-objs += camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.o

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.h b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.h
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.h
@@
 extern const struct csiphy_hw_ops csiphy_ops_2ph_1_0;
+extern const struct csiphy_hw_ops csiphy_ops_2ph_1_1;
 extern const struct csiphy_hw_ops csiphy_ops_3ph_1_0;

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ - csiphy_res_sm8150, all four entries @@
-			.hw_ops = &csiphy_ops_2ph_1_0,
+			.hw_ops = &csiphy_ops_2ph_1_1,
